   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Nigeria has the biggest upper-secondary completion gap among the 87 countries compared:** 90% of children from the richest fifth of families finished, versus 16% from the poorest fifth—a **74-percentage-point gap** in 2021.\n\nThe next largest gaps were **Laos (71 points, 2023), Ghana (68 points, 2022), Lesotho (66 points, 2024), and Zambia (64 points, 2024).**\n\nThe map uses each country’s latest matched data from 2018–2024 and excludes territories with fewer than 100,000 people. Countries without recent wealth-group data cannot be ranked.",
